			"map/gz7g": {
				"kind": "map",
				"name_key": "zone gz7g",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Two searches on the islands",
						"text": "The river islands hold two different leads. Estera needs the Orb, which Erfar places on the southernmost island. Erfar also proposes tracing [[character/bgoblinc]]’s blue Eye Stone to a possible portal. Zak takes the First Goblin’s skull to compel GoGo to visit the village; the chief explains that the orcs confiscated the written record of the stone’s origin. The islands require their own bridge mechanism, distinct from the cave’s. Zak retrieves the record and the Orb in this area. Erfar claims the record offers nothing useful, then diverts attention to missing taxes and gold in Golden Valley. His portal scheme and Estera’s search serve different purposes, even though they take Zak through the same territory.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing s6_2",
							"briefing s7_1",
							"briefing s7_4",
							"briefing s8_2",
							"briefing v5",
							"quest q7g",
							"quest q8g",
							"quest q9g",
							"quest q10g"
						],
						"event": "orb_islands",
						"order": 8
					},
					{
						"heading": "The supposed attack on the goblins",
						"text": "While Zak seeks the magician, Erfar and Gort arrange another joint operation with the Free Hunters, supposedly to prevent a goblin raid. The promised friendly meeting becomes an ambush by brigands and village soldiers. Erfar denies responsibility. Gort blames drunken, undisciplined soldiers and brigands dressed as villagers, then briefly threatens to overthrow Erfar before withdrawing the threat. Babur warns that the elder is trying to have Zak killed. A note in the newer orc script cannot yet settle the matter: Estera needs an Orc ABC Book to read it. Its translation reveals a contract on Zak’s life, a detailed description of him and a substantial payment. The search for the author becomes a separate investigation alongside the route into the Dead City.",
