			"map/gz8g": {
				"kind": "map",
				"name_key": "zone gz8g",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "The supposed attack on the goblins",
						"text": "While Zak seeks the magician, Erfar and Gort arrange another joint operation with the Free Hunters, supposedly to prevent a goblin raid. The promised friendly meeting becomes an ambush by brigands and village soldiers. Erfar denies responsibility. Gort blames drunken, undisciplined soldiers and brigands dressed as villagers, then briefly threatens to overthrow Erfar before withdrawing the threat. Babur warns that the elder is trying to have Zak killed. A note in the newer orc script cannot yet settle the matter: Estera needs an Orc ABC Book to read it. Its translation reveals a contract on Zak’s life, a detailed description of him and a substantial payment. The search for the author becomes a separate investigation alongside the route into the Dead City.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing s12_4",
							"briefing s13_0",
							"briefing m13_3",
							"briefing z13_2",
							"briefing z14",
							"quest q13ag",
							"quest q14g",
							"briefing v13_0",
							"briefing v13_1",
							"briefing v13_2"
						],
						"event": "ambush",
						"order": 12
					},
					{
						"heading": "The expedition and the Hermit’s bargain",
						"text": "Estera introduces a lost Khadaganian [[character/clerk|official]], who promises that his expedition can help Zak leave Gipath. Meeting [[character/hwleader]] instead leads to imprisonment and demands for information about a meteorite. Zak plays the ignorant swineherd, but the commander threatens torture. [[character/oliz]] offers escape on the condition that Zak later visit his home. Zak gives his word, receives the Ancient Claw for the traps on the approach and escapes. The Hermit explains that he had intended to negotiate with the armoured humans but changed his mind after seeing their treatment of Zak. Keeping the promise establishes trust where the expedition failed to do so.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing z27",
							"briefing ha29",
							"briefing ha29_1",
							"briefing ha29_2",
							"briefing ha29_3",
							"briefing l30"
						],
						"event": "expedition",
						"order": 18
					},
					{
						"heading": "The Hermit’s gift and dangerous joke",
						"text": "The Hermit offers more than directions. He gives Zak an object resembling a horn or shell, hoping it will help him survive, although he cannot explain how a human should use it. His advice about treasure is less benevolent. During their negotiations he points Zak toward the southern lizard islands and says their gold will be his. Zak can follow that lead, only to find hostile owners who pursue the intruder. When confronted, the Hermit calls the misleading invitation a joke, imitating the humour Zak had used with him. Zak makes clear that he does not find the experience amusing.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing l30",
							"briefing l30_1",
							"briefing l35",
							"quest q35g",
							"quest q35ag"
						],
						"event": "hermit_treasure",
						"order": 19
					},
					{
						"heading": "Water for the lizards and the Great Magician",
						"text": "The Hermit needs the water diverted by the orcs restored. Zak raises their dam and blocks the diversion canal; in return the lizard locates the magician in a ravine in the Remote Mountains. This information joins the tunnel instructions from the Khadaganian report. Zak passes the ancient defences and reaches [[character/rick]]. Tka-Rik explains that his dragonet has watched Zak since his unusual arrival. Bound to Gipath by his duty as its Great Magician, he offers help with Zak’s memory in exchange for bringing him two surviving young Joons. The first journey will be to Ingos to find the girl. Zak must leave his Gipath companions behind. Tka-Rik supplies an amulet for the return journey, but warns that it will work only once the girl has been found; his dragonet will travel with Zak.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing l30",
							"quest q34g",
							"briefing l34",
							"briefing z35",
							"quest q36g",
							"briefing r36",
							"briefing r36_3",
							"briefing r36_4",
							"briefing r36_2"
						],
						"event": "tka_rik",
						"order": 20
					},
					{
						"heading": "The rescue of Airy",
						"text": "Before leaving Gipath, Zak can finish the separate search for Airy, who set out to find the magician herself and impress him. Estera’s vision points to a goblin prison, where Zak finds her granddaughter’s potion bottle and a note leading to [[character/orcc]]. The orc chief intends to give Airy to a frightening armoured human he calls a Demon. Zak offers to remove this threat instead. Shei-Var first demands proof of his strength against the ogre brothers, whose wealth also threatens the chief’s influence. Once Zak defeats the Demon, Shei-Var honours his promise and sends Airy home. The rescue ends with Estera’s gratitude and Airy’s distress that Zak still regards her as a child.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing z38",
							"briefing z39",
							"briefing sh40",
							"briefing sh41",
							"briefing sh41_1",
							"briefing z41_1",
							"quest q39g",
							"quest q41g"
						],
						"event": "airy_rescue",
						"order": 22
					}
				],
				"id": "gz8g"
			},
			"map/gz4g": {
				"kind": "map",
				"name_key": "zone gz4g",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Airy’s route through the observatory",
						"text": "Airy returns with a lead to the old observatory library, but harpies occupy the site. Her plan requires a lizard’s amulet to lead a particular green dragon against them. Reaching that dragon requires Estera to freeze the lake with a green crystal. The hostile lizards on the approach present another obstacle: Zak moves the Big Shell from the Remote Mountains to the Middle Mountains, restoring the peace associated with its altar. This leaves Babur’s former quarry route unsafe and can lead to an additional errand for the craftsman. The observatory book finally supplies the password to the Dead City’s hidden entrance. Airy can also teach Zak the Magic of Feelings, only to be offended when he again calls her a little girl.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing z13_1",
							"briefing z14_1",
							"briefing m13_2",
							"briefing m15",
							"briefing z17",
							"briefing z15",
							"briefing z18",
							"quest q15ag",
							"quest q15bg",
							"quest q18g"
						],
						"event": "observatory",
						"order": 13
					},
					{
						"heading": "Reopening Babur’s quarry",
						"text": "Moving the Big Shell solves one problem and creates another. Babur can no longer use the road protected by its old altar. The alternative route passes a cyclops tending pigs stolen from the village, and the craftsman offers payment to make it safe. Zak can kill the cyclops or destroy its food supply and wait for it to leave. The latter plan depends on remaining unnoticed. Babur pays once access is restored. The dispute shows why his advice about the Shell serves his own livelihood as well as Zak’s journey.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing m15",
							"briefing m16",
							"quest q16g"
						],
						"event": "quarry",
						"order": 14
					},
					{
						"heading": "The expedition and the Hermit’s bargain",
						"text": "Estera introduces a lost Khadaganian [[character/clerk|official]], who promises that his expedition can help Zak leave Gipath. Meeting [[character/hwleader]] instead leads to imprisonment and demands for information about a meteorite. Zak plays the ignorant swineherd, but the commander threatens torture. [[character/oliz]] offers escape on the condition that Zak later visit his home. Zak gives his word, receives the Ancient Claw for the traps on the approach and escapes. The Hermit explains that he had intended to negotiate with the armoured humans but changed his mind after seeing their treatment of Zak. Keeping the promise establishes trust where the expedition failed to do so.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing z27",
							"briefing ha29",
							"briefing ha29_1",
							"briefing ha29_2",
							"briefing ha29_3",
							"briefing l30"
						],
						"event": "expedition",
						"order": 18
					},
					{
						"heading": "Water for the lizards and the Great Magician",
						"text": "The Hermit needs the water diverted by the orcs restored. Zak raises their dam and blocks the diversion canal; in return the lizard locates the magician in a ravine in the Remote Mountains. This information joins the tunnel instructions from the Khadaganian report. Zak passes the ancient defences and reaches [[character/rick]]. Tka-Rik explains that his dragonet has watched Zak since his unusual arrival. Bound to Gipath by his duty as its Great Magician, he offers help with Zak’s memory in exchange for bringing him two surviving young Joons. The first journey will be to Ingos to find the girl. Zak must leave his Gipath companions behind. Tka-Rik supplies an amulet for the return journey, but warns that it will work only once the girl has been found; his dragonet will travel with Zak.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing l30",
							"quest q34g",
							"briefing l34",
							"briefing z35",
							"quest q36g",
							"briefing r36",
							"briefing r36_3",
							"briefing r36_4",
							"briefing r36_2"
						],
						"event": "tka_rik",
						"order": 20
					}
				],
				"id": "gz4g"
			},
