			"map/gz14k": {
				"kind": "map",
				"name_key": "zone gz14k",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Lu-a-Jalla beneath the mines",
						"text": "The former punishment cell is empty. Zak follows the trail deeper into the Forbidden Catacombs until he finds [[character/deva]], who first mistakes him for another captor. She has escaped the mercenaries and found protection through the ancient treaty between Joons and Wormheads. She rejects the nickname Princess and explains that Diera imprisoned her out of jealousy over the governor. Zak falls in love with her, but she remains faithful to At-Zako, who drew the Joon Curse away from her. Zak promises to respect that bond. They return to Tka-Rik, and the next mission becomes the search for her missing beloved on Suslanger.",
						"sources": [
							"quest q55k",
							"briefing d55",
							"briefing d55_1",
							"briefing d55_3",
							"briefing r54"
						],
						"event": "lua",
						"order": 27
					}
				],
				"id": "gz14k"
			},
			"map/gz15h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"name_key": "zone gz15h",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Captivity in Death Canyon",
						"text": "Zak is captured near the portal on [[allod/suslanger]]. Lieutenant [[character/karh]] presents him to [[character/iz]], who orders him used as live quarry for soldiers seeking promotion. Surviving the run through Death Canyon earns only a return to captivity, not freedom. Kardaur threatens punishment through necromancy if Zak dies too quickly and displeases his superior.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing hns59",
							"quest q60h"
						],
						"event": "canyon",
						"order": 29
					},
					{
						"heading": "The Odalisque and the escape",
						"text": "The [[character/nalo]] approaches Zak after his ordeal. Enslaved by Kardaur and deprived even of a personal name, she wants his death and knows he will guard the gate that night. She steals the key to Zak’s cage. Her father, a rat hunter who disappeared in the caves, told her of the Wormheads’ temple and the bridges across its lava rivers. She uses that knowledge to explain a route the guards fear to follow. Zak kills Kardaur for the fortress key and escapes toward the cave; releasing the caged spiders can delay pursuit. The Odalisque and Zak part with wishes for each other’s freedom and survival, without a stated account of her later fate.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing kr60",
							"briefing kr61",
							"quest q61h",
							"quest q62h",
							"quest q63h"
						],
						"event": "odalisque",
						"order": 30
					}
				],
				"id": "gz15h"
			},
			"map/gz16h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"name_key": "zone gz16h",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "The Odalisque and the escape",
						"text": "The [[character/nalo]] approaches Zak after his ordeal. Enslaved by Kardaur and deprived even of a personal name, she wants his death and knows he will guard the gate that night. She steals the key to Zak’s cage. Her father, a rat hunter who disappeared in the caves, told her of the Wormheads’ temple and the bridges across its lava rivers. She uses that knowledge to explain a route the guards fear to follow. Zak kills Kardaur for the fortress key and escapes toward the cave; releasing the caged spiders can delay pursuit. The Odalisque and Zak part with wishes for each other’s freedom and survival, without a stated account of her later fate.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing kr60",
							"briefing kr61",
							"quest q61h",
							"quest q62h",
							"quest q63h"
						],
						"event": "odalisque",
						"order": 30
					},
					{
						"heading": "Acceptance into the Last Shelter",
						"text": "Beyond the caves, [[character/kuzn]] finds Zak and vouches for him before [[character/glav]]. The brotherhood’s leader fears imperial spies and requires the Emperor’s Signet Ring, taken from a cyclops who killed its courier. Possessing such an object compromises the newcomer with the authorities and makes the test more than a feat of strength. After Zak returns, Khatul accepts him as Brother Blondie and offers the refuge as a new home. Zak explains his promise to find At-Zako and return to Gipath. Khatul respects that purpose and asks those who can help to support him; [[character/guru]] can teach him greater dexterity.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing gl63",
							"briefing gl64",
							"briefing guru1"
						],
						"event": "shelter",
						"order": 31
					}
				],
				"id": "gz16h"
			},
			"map/gz17h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"name_key": "zone gz17h",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Acceptance into the Last Shelter",
						"text": "Beyond the caves, [[character/kuzn]] finds Zak and vouches for him before [[character/glav]]. The brotherhood’s leader fears imperial spies and requires the Emperor’s Signet Ring, taken from a cyclops who killed its courier. Possessing such an object compromises the newcomer with the authorities and makes the test more than a feat of strength. After Zak returns, Khatul accepts him as Brother Blondie and offers the refuge as a new home. Zak explains his promise to find At-Zako and return to Gipath. Khatul respects that purpose and asks those who can help to support him; [[character/guru]] can teach him greater dexterity.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing gl63",
							"briefing gl64",
							"briefing guru1"
						],
						"event": "shelter",
						"order": 31
					},
					{
						"heading": "The Blacksmith’s revenge and Kehel’s experiment",
						"text": "The Shelter’s inhabitants can ask for help with their own grievances alongside the search for At-Zako. Brother Blacksmith wants the slavedriver brothers Lash-Aga and Whip-Aga killed at the plantations. If Zak carries out the request, the workers raise the alarm instead of helping him. The smith explains that imperial law threatens them with death if they fail to report a stranger, then promises to repay the revenge. Kehel offers a separate commission: destroy a harpy he once experimented on, so rivals cannot claim his work. After its death, he admits that fear of Zak’s strength is what makes him honour the promised reward. Their requests expose different consequences of life under the empire: coerced obedience among the workers, personal revenge among its fugitives, and rivalry among its scholars.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing kuz64_2",
							"briefing kuz64_3",
							"briefing ne64_2",
							"briefing ne64_3",
							"quest q64ah",
							"quest qk31h"
						],
						"event": "shelter_revenge",
						"order": 32
					},
					{
						"heading": "Kholai and the dead scientist",
						"text": "[[character/nekro]] directs Zak to [[character/oldnekro]], whom Taivo displaced from the imperial laboratory. Kholai wants disgrace for his rival rather than a simple assassination. Zak steals a dead scientist’s head from the laboratory; its disappearance will embarrass Taivo, and Kholai can summon its spirit. The [[character/spirit|scientist]] describes a horror pursuing the red-skinned youth. To conceal him, the scholars changed his appearance and sent him away by teleportation. Kholai interprets the broken testimony and tells Zak to search the ruined mansion for the magical object used in the escape. The fragments Zak finds are beyond Kehel’s ability to interpret: only a Great Magician can identify the destination. Kholai can also give Zak an experimental object to test in combat. He is interested in the result even if the trial kills its user, a further sign of the limits of his concern for his visitor.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing ne67",
							"briefing sn67",
							"quest q69h",
							"briefing sn69",
							"briefing sn69_1",
							"quest q70h",
							"briefing ne70",
							"briefing sn67_1"
						],
						"event": "spirit",
						"order": 35
					}
				],
				"id": "gz17h"
			},
