			"character/merc7": {
				"kind": "character",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Overview",
						"text": "[[character/merc7]] is a thief associated with Aliya and the Last Shelter. Her disappearance leads to a rescue and a search for medicine. Once recovered, she helps the travellers with forged enlistment papers in exchange for recovering a hidden cache, opening a route into imperial service.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing brief_47",
							"briefing brief_48",
							"briefing brief_59a",
							"briefing brief_59b"
						]
					},
					{
						"heading": "The ring and the brotherhood",
						"text": "Khatul demands an imperial signet ring from a cyclops as a test of trust. Kir brings it back and explains his intention to free his family. He also recognises that the ring does not match the description he has read. Khatul already knows it is false, but asks him to preserve the brotherhood’s belief in the trophy. Membership changes how [[character/zaku]] receives Kir: the smith who refused a stranger now offers his craft. Through Aliya, Kir also searches for the missing [[character/merc7]], rescues her and brings medicine. Sahilia’s recovery matters later, when her forged papers open a route into the army.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing brief_43",
							"briefing brief_43a",
							"briefing brief_44",
							"briefing brief_45",
							"briefing brief_46",
							"briefing brief_47",
							"briefing brief_48",
							"briefing brief_59a"
						],
						"event": "brotherhood",
						"order": 9
					},
					{
						"heading": "The report and the passage to Gipath",
						"text": "Karim locates a report about the missing red-skinned youth in the necromancers’ citadel. He has bribed a guard to open the gate and get the other guards drunk, but the watch remains alert. Kir and Kel retrieve the document despite the failed arrangement, and Kir defends Karim when Kel blames him. The report records transformation and teleportation before the attack on the scholars’ mansion, with Gipath as the destination. Kir decides to follow that Joon. Sahilia initially warns against joining the army, then has convincing enlistment papers forged while Kir empties her dangerous caches for her. Kel refuses to be left behind, passing as a young man herself. [[character/sergant]] puts them through military training in Death Canyon. Their performance earns a courier assignment to the Gipath expedition. Sealed orders and a portal pass finally let them leave Suslanger under the authority of the same empire that enslaved them.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing brief_31",
							"briefing brief_82",
							"briefing brief_83",
							"briefing brief_59a",
							"briefing brief_86",
