			"character/firez": {
				"kind": "character",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Overview",
						"text": "[[character/firez]] rules the Khadaganian side of Jigran and is the enemy Kir fled. In their confrontation he reveals that he too is a Joon, expelled for necromancy, and claims that his experiments were meant to defeat the Curse. He prolongs his life at Jigran’s expense, tracks Kir with a dragonet and threatens to turn him into an obedient undead servant. His professed concern for the Joons sits beside his enslavement and coercion of them.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing brief_119",
							"briefing brief_349"
						]
					},
					{
						"heading": "Escape from Jigran",
						"text": "[[character/hero]], whose full name is Kir-A-Chit-La, is a young Joon enslaved under [[character/firez]] on [[allod/jigran]]. He escapes the castle, leaving his family behind, and hopes to return with help. Outside the castle, a [[character/first|recruiter]] mistakes him for someone expected at the camp. Kir conceals his identity and accepts travel papers for work on Suslanger. The apparent opening to freedom instead delivers him to imperial authorities. [[character/hwleader]] dismisses his papers, treats him as a slave and considers reporting the red-skinned stranger for a reward.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing brief_0",
							"briefing brief_1",
							"briefing brief_119",
							"zone gz1g"
						],
						"event": "flight",
						"order": 1
					},
					{
						"heading": "Firez’s identity and the final confrontation",
						"text": "In the throne room, Firez reveals that he too is a Joon and has watched Kir through a dragonet since the escape. He says his people expelled him for necromancy and claims that his rule protected them from the Curse. Kir answers with their enslavement, his parents’ deaths and the destruction of Jigran to prolong Firez’s life. The tyrant’s explanation is his own defence, not proof that the captivity was benevolent. He threatens to kill Kir, raise him as an obedient servant and use him against the baron. Their exchange leads into the final battle for Jigran. Firez shelters behind a lethal magical barrier. Kir disables its four controls before he can reach the necromancer; teleportation platforms and enchanted lion statues form part of the final arena. Killing Firez completes the last quest and ends the campaign.",
						"sources": [
							"briefing brief_349",
							"zone gz36j",
							"quest q22j",
							"script zonefinal"
						],
						"event": "firez",
						"order": 44
					}
				],
				"actors": [
					"firez"
				],
				"name_key": "pers firez",
				"id": "firez",
				"placements": [
					{
						"zone": "cz4j",
						"actor": "firez",
						"prototype": "zonefinal jun firez m"
					}
				],
				"prototypes": [
					"zonefinal jun firez m"
				],
